  "wikipedia": {
    "title": "Eta Geminorum",
    "description": "Star in the constellation Gemini",
    "summary": "Eta Geminorum, formally named Propus, is a triple star system in the constellation of Gemini. It is a variable star visible to the naked eye, around 380 light years from the Sun. The position of this system near the ecliptic means it is subject to lunar occultation.",
    "intro": "Eta Geminorum (η Geminorum, abbreviated Eta Gem, η Gem), formally named Propus , is a triple star system in the constellation of Gemini. It is a variable star visible to the naked eye, around 380 light years from the Sun. The position of this system near the ecliptic means it is subject to lunar occultation.",
